        "summary": "OH atrial fibrillation cases tied to Concomitant Left Atrial Appendage Closure and Cardiac Ablation added about +$5.2M, including 94 more admissions across two AF diagnoses. OH Medicare HMO acute hospital spend for the same procedure added about +$3.1M on 61 more admissions with about +$8.0K higher paid per admit. IN added about +$1.3M and NY about +$1.2M for the same procedure, showing the pattern is spreading beyond OH. ADVOCATE SOUTH SUBURBAN HOSPITAL appears in both OH and IN as a smaller but recurring concentration point."
      }
